# Machine registry: prod machines only.
# This file is private data, kept in the private config repo and injected into
# etc/ by fetch-private-data via .private-source (see
# doc/system/private-config.md). `pf-deploy.sh` and `deploy-private-config`
# read the [prod] roster (locally, on the deploy machine — `machines.ini` is
# never shipped to a host); the dev-machine `DBUSER` mapping now lives in
# etc/team.ini (see etc/team.ini.template), not here.
#
# [prod] prod deploy targets. Each key is the server's ZeroTier IP (the same
#        address `pf-deploy.sh` uses for SSH). The value is a comma-separated
#        list of `tag[:name]` tokens:
#          named tag   `db:simo0` -> a `db` resource named `simo0`
#          bare tag    `worker`   -> boolean flag (install cron on this host)
#        `db` (named) and `worker` (bare) are the framework's built-in tags:
#        a `db:<name>` token names a database and enforces the one-to-one
#        server mapping (the instance itself is provisioned by `ema create`;
#        db-check verifies it via the host's own `mariadb@*` units, not this
#        roster); `worker` installs the `cron-manifest` output (cron jobs) on
#        every deploy. Every other tag is consumer-owned:
#          `web`     restore Apache www-data traversal on the repo dir
#        A host with a `db:<name>` token is a database host; a bare `worker`
#        token adds cron install on that host; an empty value is a code-only
#        server (it deploys the codebase but runs no tagged step).
#
#        Service-account pins — the framework `gen-service-accounts` CLI
#        reconciles passwordless host-pinned accounts and roles from the
#        shared srv/roles-<GUID> declaration plus etc/team.ini (the `member`
#        source) and this roster. Each token is a role-pin source: `worker`
#        -> `simox_worker`, every `db:<name>` -> `simox_db`, `web` ->
#        `simox_web` (see README "Service Accounts"). Removing a tag (or a
#        whole host) here revokes the corresponding role on the next
#        reconcile; the `member` IPs come from etc/team.ini, not here.
#
#        Constraint: a named token may appear on exactly ONE server
#        (`db:simo0` and `db:simo1` are independent databases; `web` is
#        independent of both). Bare flags carry no name, hence no uniqueness
#        constraint. A server may host no database (code-only), one database,
#        or several databases (one MariaDB instance each, created by
#        `ema create`).

[prod]
# 10.147.x.10=db:simo0, worker
# 10.147.x.11=db:simo1, web
